# 9. Elastic Network Interface (ENI)

An ENI is a virtual network card.

Each EC2 instance has:

```text
EC2 Node

|

Primary ENI

|

Secondary ENIs

|

Pod IP Addresses
```

---

Example:

```text
Worker Node


eth0

10.0.1.10


eth1

10.0.1.20


eth2

10.0.1.21
```

---

# 10. ENI Limits

Every EC2 instance has limits:

* Number of ENIs
* Number of IP addresses per ENI

Example:

Small instance:

```text
Few ENIs

Few Pods
```

Large instance:

```text
More ENIs

More Pods
```

This affects EKS node sizing.

---

# 11. Prefix Delegation

VPC CNI supports prefix delegation.

Instead of assigning individual IPs:

```text
Old:

ENI

IP
IP
IP
```

New:

```text
ENI

Prefix

10.0.1.0/28
```

Benefits:

* More Pod IP capacity
* Faster scaling

