# 15. Kubernetes Networking Model

Kubernetes networking has three main requirements:

## Requirement 1

Every Pod gets an IP.

Example:

```text
Pod A

10.0.1.20
```

---

## Requirement 2

Pods communicate directly.

Example:

```text
Pod A

↓

Pod B
```

---

## Requirement 3

Containers inside a Pod share networking.

Example:

```text
Pod

10.0.1.20

|

Container A

Container B
```

---

# 16. Kubernetes Service Networking

Pods are temporary.

Example:

```text
Pod

10.0.1.20


Restart


Pod

10.0.1.30
```

Service provides stable access.

Architecture:

```text
Client

↓

Service IP

↓

Pod IP
```

---

