# 27. EKS Networking Troubleshooting

## Check Pod IP

```bash
kubectl get pods -o wide
```

---

## Check Services

```bash
kubectl get svc
```

---

## Check Endpoints

```bash
kubectl get endpoints
```

---

## Check DNS

Enter Pod:

```bash
kubectl exec -it pod-name -- bash
```

Test:

```bash
nslookup kubernetes.default
```

---

## Check Network Policies

```bash
kubectl get networkpolicy
```

---

# 28. Common Networking Problems

## Problem: Pod cannot access internet

Check:

* NAT Gateway
* Route tables
* Security groups

---

## Problem: Service has no endpoints

Check:

```bash
kubectl get endpoints
```

Possible cause:

* Label mismatch
* Pods not ready

---

## Problem: Load Balancer not created

Check:

* AWS Load Balancer Controller
* IAM permissions
* Subnet tags

---

